            - API Server CPU
            - Network bandwidth
            - Memory
            - etcd resources
            
            Clearly, Kubernetes needed a better solution.
            
            ---
            
            # The Problem
            
            Suppose a cluster has:
            
            ```text
            200,000 Pods
            ```
            
            Each Pod object occupies roughly:
            
            ```text
            5 KB
            ```
            
            One cache:
            
            ```text
            200,000 × 5 KB
            
            ≈ 1 GB
            ```
            
            If there are:
            
            ```text
            20 Controllers
            ```
            
            Each maintaining its own cache:
            
            ```text
            20 GB
            ```
            
            of duplicated memory.
            
            Now add:
            
            - LIST operations
            - WATCH streams
            - Object deserialization
            
            The cluster quickly becomes inefficient.
            
            ---
            
            # Kubernetes Solution
            
            Instead of every controller creating its own Informer,
            
            Kubernetes introduced:
            
            ```text
            Shared Informers
            ```
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            One LIST
            
            ↓
            
            One WATCH
            
            ↓
            
            One Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Many Controllers
            ```
            
            This dramatically reduces duplication.
            
            ---
            
            # High-Level Architecture
            
            ```text
                               API Server
            
                                   │
            
                             LIST + WATCH
            
                                   │
            
                             Shared Informer
            
                                   │
            
                             Shared Cache
            
                                   │
            
                  ┌──────────┬──────────┬──────────┐
            
                  ▼          ▼          ▼          ▼
            
             Deployment   HPA      Scheduler   Operator
             Controller
            ```
            
            Every controller reads the same cache.
            
            ---
            
            # What is a Shared Informer?
            
            A Shared Informer is an Informer whose:
            
            - LIST
            - WATCH
            - Reflector
            - DeltaFIFO
            - Local Cache
            
            are shared among multiple consumers.
            
            Instead of each controller building its own synchronization pipeline,
            
            all controllers reuse the same pipeline.
            
            ---
            
            # SharedInformerFactory
            
            Creating multiple independent Informers manually would still create duplication.
            
            Instead,
            
            `client-go` provides:
            
            ```go
            SharedInformerFactory
            ```
            
            Its job is to create and manage Shared Informers.
            
            Think of it as:
            
            ```text
            Informer Manager
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # SharedInformerFactory Architecture
            
            ```text
            SharedInformerFactory
            
            │
            
            ├── Pod Informer
            
            ├── Deployment Informer
            
            ├── Secret Informer
            
            ├── Service Informer
            
            ├── Node Informer
            
            └── ConfigMap Informer
            ```
            
            Each resource type has exactly one Shared Informer.
            
            ---
            
            # Workflow
            
            Suppose:
            
            Deployment Controller asks:
            
            ```go
            PodInformer()
            ```
            
            Later,
            
            HPA asks:
            
            ```go
            PodInformer()
            ```
            
            The factory does **not** create another one.
            
            Instead:
            
            ```text
            Return Existing Informer
            ```
            
            Everyone shares it.
            
            ---
            
            # SharedIndexInformer
            
            The most commonly used Informer implementation is:
            
            ```go
            SharedIndexInformer
            ```
            
            It combines:
            
            ```text
            Reflector
            
            +
            
            DeltaFIFO
            
            +
            
            Indexer
            
            +
            
            Shared Cache
            
            +
            
            Event Distribution
            ```
            
            into one reusable component.
            
            ---
            
            # Internal Components
            
            ```text
            SharedIndexInformer
            
            │
            
            ├── Reflector
            
            ├── DeltaFIFO
            
            ├── Shared Cache
            
            ├── Shared Indexer
            
            ├── Event Broadcaster
            
            └── Event Handlers
            ```
            
            Notice:
            
            There is still only **one** Reflector.
            
            ---
            
            # Shared Cache
            
            The Shared Cache stores one copy of every object.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Pod nginx
            
            Running
            
            Node worker-1
            
            Labels app=web
            ```
            
            Deployment Controller reads it.
            
            ↓
            
            HPA reads the same object.
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduler reads the same object.
            
            No duplication.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Workflow
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Reflector
            
            ↓
            
            DeltaFIFO
            
            ↓
            
            Shared Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Controller A
            
            ↓
            
            Controller B
            
            ↓
            
            Controller C
            ```
            
            Every controller sees identical cluster state.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Synchronization
            
            Startup sequence:
            
            ```text
            LIST
            
            ↓
            
            Populate Shared Cache
            
            ↓
            
            WaitForCacheSync()
            
            ↓
            
            Controllers Start
            ```
            
            All controllers wait for the cache to become consistent before reconciling resources.
            
            ---
            
            # Shared Indexer
            
            Searching the cache by scanning every object would be slow.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Find:
            
            Pods
            
            Running
            
            On worker-5
            ```
            
            Scanning:
            
            ```text
            200,000 Pods
            ```
            
            for every query is inefficient.
            
            ---
            
            # Kubernetes Solution
            
            The cache includes an **Indexer**.
            
            Think of it like a database index.
            
            Instead of searching every object,
            
            the Indexer provides direct lookup paths.
            
            ---
            
            # Real-Life Analogy
            
            Imagine a phone book.
            
            Without an index:
            
            ```text
            Read
            
            Page 1
            
            ↓
            
            Page 2
            
            ↓
            
            Page 3
            
            ...
            ```
            
            With an alphabetical index:
            
            ```text
            Go directly to:
            
            "K"
            ```
            
            Much faster.
            
            The Shared Indexer works the same way.
            
            ---
            
            # What Does the Shared Indexer Store?
            
            It stores references to cached objects using keys.
            
            Default key:
            
            ```text
            namespace/name
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            default/nginx
            
            ↓
            
            Pod Object
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Default Index
            
            Most Informers use:
            
            ```text
            Namespace
            
            ↓
            
            Object Name
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            default/nginx
            
            kube-system/coredns
            
            production/api
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Custom Indexes
            
            Developers can define custom indexes.
            
            Examples:
            
            Index by:
            
            ```text
            Node
            
            Labels
            
            OwnerReference
            
            ServiceAccount
            
            StorageClass
            ```
            
            This enables extremely fast lookups.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Instead of:
            
            ```text
            Find Pods on worker-3
            
            ↓
            
            Scan Entire Cache
            ```
            
            The Indexer performs:
            
            ```text
            worker-3
            
            ↓
            
            Direct Lookup
            
            ↓
            
            Matching Pods
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Event Distribution
            
            When a Watch event arrives:
            
            ```text
            MODIFIED
            
            ↓
            
            Update Shared Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Notify Every Registered Handler
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Deployment Controller
            
            ↓
            
            HPA
            
            ↓
            
            Operator
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduler
            ```
            
            One event,
            
            many consumers.
            
            ---
            
