            # Cache
            
            The Cache in controller-runtime is built on top of client-go Shared Informers.
            
            It stores:
            
            ```text
            Pods
            
            Deployments
            
            Services
            
            Secrets
            
            Nodes
            
            CRDs
            ```
            
            The Cache continuously synchronizes with the API Server.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Architecture
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Watch
            
            ↓
            
            Shared Informers
            
            ↓
            
            Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Controllers
            ```
            
            Controllers rarely read directly from the API Server.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Cache?
            
            Suppose reconciliation needs:
            
            ```text
            500 Pods
            ```
            
            Without cache:
            
            ```text
            500 API Calls
            ```
            
            With cache:
            
            ```text
            Memory Lookup
            ```
            
            Huge performance improvement.
            
            ---
            
            # Client
            
            controller-runtime provides a unified Client.
            
            Unlike client-go,
            
            you usually don't work with:
            
            ```go
            Clientset
            ```
            
            Instead:
            
            ```go
            client.Client
            ```
            
            One interface supports:
            
            - Get
            - List
            - Create
            - Update
            - Patch
            - Delete
            
            ---
            
            # Client Architecture
            
            ```text
            Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Client
            
            ├── Read
            
            └── Write
            ```
            
            But there is an important detail.
            
            ---
            
            # Split Client
            
            The default controller-runtime Client is a **Split Client**.
            
            Reads:
            
            ```text
            Cache
            ```
            
            Writes:
            
            ```text
            API Server
            ```
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Get()
            
            ↓
            
            Cache
            
            -------------------
            
            Update()
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            ```
            
            This combines:
            
            - Fast reads
            - Strongly consistent writes
            
            ---
            
            # Why Split Reads and Writes?
            
            Imagine:
            
            ```text
            Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Get Deployment
            ```
            
            Using cache:
            
            ```text
            Memory
            
            ↓
            
            Microseconds
            ```
            
            Later:
            
            ```text
            Update Deployment
            ```
            
            Must go through:
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Validation
            
            ↓
            
            Admission
            
            ↓
            
            etcd
