            # Concurrency Problem
            
            Imagine:
            
            Two controllers.
            
            Both read:
            
            ```yaml
            replicas: 3
            ```
            
            Controller A:
            
            ```text
            Scale To 5
            ```
            
            Controller B:
            
            ```text
            Scale To 10
            ```
            
            Without concurrency control:
            
            Last writer wins.
            
            One update disappears.
            
            ---
            
            # Optimistic Concurrency
            
            Instead of locking,
            
            MVCC assumes conflicts are rare.
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Read Object
            
            ↓
            
            Remember Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Modify
            
            ↓
            
            Write
            
            ↓
            
            Revision Still Same?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Success
            
            ------------------
            
            No
            
            ↓
            
            Conflict
            ```
            
            This is called:
            
            ```text
            Optimistic Concurrency Control
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why "Optimistic"?
            
            Because the system optimistically assumes:
            
            ```text
            Nobody Else
            
            Changed
            
            The Object
            ```
            
            Most Kubernetes objects are not modified simultaneously.
            
            So this approach is efficient.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Controller A reads:
            
            ```text
            Revision 100
            ```
            
            Controller B updates.
            
            Current revision:
            
            ```text
            101
            ```
            
            Controller A attempts update.
            
            Server checks:
            
            ```text
            Expected
            
            100
            
            Current
            
            101
            ```
            
            Mismatch.
            
            Update rejected.
            
            ---
            
            # Conflict Detection
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            Read Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Modify
            
            ↓
            
            Send Update
            
            ↓
            
            Revision Match?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Commit
            
            -----------------
            
            No
            
            ↓
            
            409 Conflict
            ```
            
            The client must:
            
            - Re-read the object
            - Apply its changes again
            - Retry the update
            
            ---
            
            # Transactions
            
            MVCC supports atomic transactions.
            
            Multiple operations become:
            
            ```text
            One
            
            Atomic
            
            Unit
            ```
            
            Either:
            
            ```text
            Everything Succeeds
            ```
            
            Or:
            
            ```text
            Nothing Happens
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Transaction Components
            
            An etcd transaction consists of:
            
            ```text
            Compare
            
            ↓
            
            Then
            
            ↓
            
            Else
            ```
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```text
            IF condition
            
            THEN operations
            
            ELSE alternate operations
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Transaction Workflow
            
            ```text
            Compare Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Matches?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Execute Writes
            
            ↓
            
            Commit
            
            -------------------
            
            No
            
            ↓
            
            Execute Failure Path
            ```
            
            Everything is atomic.
            
            ---
            
            # Compare-And-Swap (CAS)
            
            CAS is one of the most common transaction patterns.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            IF
            
            Version == 5
            
            THEN
            
            Update Value
            
            ELSE
            
            Reject
            ```
            
            No race conditions.
            
            ---
            
            # CAS Example
            
            Current:
            
            ```text
            Version = 4
            ```
            
            Client expects:
            
            ```text
            Version = 4
            ```
            
            Update succeeds.
            
            Another client:
            
            ```text
            Version = 4
            ```
            
            But current:
            
            ```text
            Version = 5
            ```
            
            Update fails.
            
            Conflict detected.
            
            ---
            
            # Why CAS Matters
            
            Suppose two controllers try to become leader.
            
            Without CAS:
            
            ```text
            Controller A
            
            Leader
            
            ------------
            
            Controller B
            
            Leader
            ```
            
            With CAS:
            
            Only one successfully updates the shared key.
            
            Leader election becomes safe.
            
            ---
            
            # Kubernetes Update Workflow
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```bash
            kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
            ```
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Read Object
            
            ↓
            
            Current Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Apply Changes
            
            ↓
            
            Compare Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Match?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Update etcd
            
            ↓
            
            New Revision
            
            ↓
            
            Return Success
            ```
            
            If another client updated the object first,
            
            the update fails with a conflict.
            
