            # Why Should You Learn Leases?
            
            One of the most common Kubernetes interview questions is:
            
            > **How does Kubernetes know when a Node is dead?**
            
            Or,
            
            > **How does Leader Election work without manually releasing locks?**
            
            Or,
            
            > **How are temporary resources automatically cleaned up?**
            
            The answer begins with:
            
            ```text
            Leases
            ```
            
            Without leases:
            
            - Dead nodes would appear alive forever.
            - Distributed locks could remain locked permanently.
            - Failed leaders could never be replaced.
            - Temporary resources would accumulate indefinitely.
            
            Leases allow etcd to automatically clean up stale state.
            
            ---
            
            # The Problem Without Leases
            
            Imagine:
            
            A process registers itself.
            
            ```text
            Service A
            
            ↓
            
            "I'm Alive"
            ```
            
            Then:
            
            ```text
            Machine Crashes
            ```
            
            The registration remains forever.
            
            Other systems still believe:
            
            ```text
            Service A
            
            Is Running
            ```
            
            Even though it no longer exists.
            
            ---
            
            # Solution
            
            Instead of permanent registration:
            
            ```text
            Register
            
            ↓
            
            Lease
            
            ↓
            
            Renew Periodically
            
            ↓
            
            Automatic Removal
            ```
            
            If the process disappears,
            
            the lease expires,
            
            and etcd removes the associated keys automatically.
            
            ---
            
            # What is a Lease?
            
            A Lease is:
            
            > **A time-limited ownership contract between a client and one or more keys.**
            
            Think of it as:
            
            ```text
            Temporary Ownership
            ```
            
            A key attached to a lease exists only while the lease remains valid.
            
            ---
            
            # Real-Life Analogy
            
            Imagine renting a parking space.
            
            You receive:
            
            ```text
            Parking Permit
            
            Valid
            
            30 Days
            ```
            
            If you renew:
            
            ```text
            Continue Parking
            ```
            
            If you forget:
            
            ```text
            Permit Expires
            
            ↓
            
            Parking Rights Lost
            ```
            
            An etcd lease works the same way.
            
            ---
            
            # Lease Architecture
            
            ```text
                         Client
            
                           │
            
                  Create Lease
            
                           │
            
                           ▼
            
                      Lease Manager
            
                           │
            
                  Lease ID + TTL
            
                           │
            
                           ▼
            
                      Attach Keys
            
                           │
            
                     KeepAlive
            
                           │
            
                           ▼
            
                     Lease Active
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Not Just Delete Keys Manually?
            
            Imagine:
            
            ```text
            Application
            
            ↓
            
            Create Session
            
            ↓
            
            Crash
            ```
            
            Manual cleanup never happens.
            
            The database accumulates stale entries.
            
            Leases automate cleanup even when applications fail unexpectedly.
            
            ---
            
            # Lease ID
            
            Every lease has a unique identifier.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Lease ID
            
            1001
            ```
            
            Another:
            
            ```text
            Lease ID
            
            1002
            ```
            
            The Lease ID uniquely identifies the lease,
            
            not the attached keys.
            
            ---
            
            # One Lease, Multiple Keys
            
            One lease may own multiple keys.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Lease ID
            
            500
            ```
            
            Attached:
            
            ```text
            /service/web
            
            /service/web/ip
            
            /service/web/port
            ```
            
            When the lease expires,
            
            all attached keys are removed together.
            
            ---
            
            # Lease Relationship
            
            ```text
            Lease 100
            
                  │
            
             ┌────┼────┐
            
             ▼    ▼    ▼
            
            Key1 Key2 Key3
            ```
            
            One lease.
            
            Many keys.
            
            ---
            
            # Time-To-Live (TTL)
            
            Every lease has:
            
            ```text
            TTL
            
            (Time-To-Live)
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            TTL = 30 Seconds
            ```
            
            Meaning:
            
            ```text
            Lease Valid
            
            For
            
            30 Seconds
            ```
            
            Unless renewed.
            
            ---
            
            # TTL Countdown
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            30
            
            ↓
            
            29
            
            ↓
            
            28
            
            ↓
            
            ...
            
            ↓
            
            2
            
            ↓
            
            1
            
            ↓
            
            Expired
            ```
            
            Once TTL reaches zero,
            
            the lease expires.
            
            ---
            
            # Creating a Lease
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            Request Lease
            
            ↓
            
            TTL = 60 Seconds
            
            ↓
            
            Server Allocates
            
            Lease ID = 101
            
            ↓
            
            Lease Created
            ```
            
            The lease exists independently of keys.
            
            ---
            
            # Attaching Keys
            
            Now attach a key.
            
            ```text
            Lease 101
            
            ↓
            
            Attach
            
            ↓
            
            /sessions/user123
            ```
            
            Now:
            
            ```text
            Key Lifetime
            
            =
            
            Lease Lifetime
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Lease Lifecycle
            
            ```text
            Create Lease
            
            ↓
            
            Attach Keys
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            Lease Active
            ```
            
            If renewals stop:
            
            ```text
            TTL
            
            ↓
            
            0
            
            ↓
            
            Expired
            
            ↓
            
            Keys Deleted
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # KeepAlive
            
            A lease must be renewed before it expires.
            
            This renewal is called:
            
            ```text
            KeepAlive
            ```
            
            Think of it as saying:
            
            ```text
            "I'm Still Alive"
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # KeepAlive Workflow
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            Lease Timer Reset
            
            ↓
            
            TTL Returns To Full Value
            ```
            
            The countdown starts again.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            TTL:
            
            ```text
            10 Seconds
            ```
            
            Timeline:
            
            ```text
            10
            
            ↓
            
            9
            
            ↓
            
            8
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            10
            
            ↓
            
            9
            
            ↓
            
            8
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            10
            ```
            
            The lease never expires while KeepAlive messages continue.
            
            ---
            
            # Continuous Renewal
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            Server
            
            ↓
            
            Lease Extended
            
            ↓
            
            Repeat Forever
            ```
            
            As long as communication continues,
            
            the lease remains valid.
            
            ---
            
            # What Happens if KeepAlive Stops?
            
            Suppose:
            
            Application crashes.
            
            ```text
            KeepAlive Stops
            ```
            
            TTL continues.
            
            ```text
            5
            
            ↓
            
            4
            
            ↓
            
            3
            
            ↓
            
            2
            
            ↓
            
            1
            
            ↓
            
            0
            ```
            
            Lease expires.
            
            ---
            
            # Automatic Expiration
            
            When TTL reaches zero:
            
            ```text
            Lease
            
            ↓
            
            Expired
            
            ↓
            
            Delete Attached Keys
            
            ↓
            
            Generate Watch Events
            ```
            
            Cleanup happens automatically.
            
            No application intervention is required.
            
            ---
            
            # Expiration Workflow
            
            ```text
            Application Crash
            
            ↓
            
            No KeepAlive
            
            ↓
            
            TTL Expires
            
            ↓
            
            Lease Removed
            
            ↓
            
            Keys Deleted
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Events Sent
            ```
            
            Everything is automatic.
            
            ---
            
            # Internal Lease Architecture
            
            ```text
                           Lease Manager
            
                                 │
            
                  ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
            
                  ▼              ▼              ▼
            
             Lease ID         TTL Timer     Attached Keys
            
                  │
            
                  ▼
            
            Expiration Queue
            
                  │
            
                  ▼
            
            Delete Keys
            ```
            
            The Lease Manager continuously checks for expired leases.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Watches Matter
            
            Remember the previous chapter.
            
            Lease expires.
            
            Keys disappear.
            
            Immediately:
            
            ```text
            DELETE Event
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Stream
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Informer
            
            ↓
            
            Controller
            ```
            
            Expiration is visible throughout Kubernetes.
            
