            # Understanding Fragmentation
            
            Suppose a database contains:
            
            ```text
            Page 1
            
            Page 2
            
            Page 3
            
            Page 4
            
            Page 5
            ```
            
            Delete data inside:
            
            ```text
            Page 2
            
            Page 4
            ```
            
            Now:
            
            ```text
            Page1
            
            Empty
            
            Page3
            
            Empty
            
            Page5
            ```
            
            The empty pages still occupy disk space.
            
            This is:
            
            ```text
            Fragmentation
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # What is Disk Fragmentation?
            
            Disk fragmentation means:
            
            > **The database file contains unused internal space that is no longer storing active data but is still allocated on disk.**
            
            The file size remains unchanged.
            
            Unused pages remain inside the file.
            
            ---
            
            # Internal View
            
            Before:
            
            ```text
            +---------------------------+
            
            DATA
            
            DATA
            
            DATA
            
            DATA
            
            DATA
            
            +---------------------------+
            ```
            
            After many deletions:
            
            ```text
            +---------------------------+
            
            DATA
            
            EMPTY
            
            DATA
            
            EMPTY
            
            DATA
            
            +---------------------------+
            ```
            
            The file is the same size.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Fragmentation Happens
            
            Remember MVCC.
            
            Every update creates:
            
            ```text
            New Version
            ```
            
            Compaction later removes:
            
            ```text
            Old Version
            ```
            
            The old pages become:
            
            ```text
            Free Pages
            ```
            
            But the file itself is not rewritten.
            
            ---
            
            # Continuous Lifecycle
            
            ```text
            Write
            
            ↓
            
            Update
            
            ↓
            
            MVCC History
            
            ↓
            
            Compaction
            
            ↓
            
            Free Pages
            
            ↓
            
            More Writes
            
            ↓
            
            More Free Pages
            ```
            
            Over time,
            
            fragmentation increases.
            
