            - Slow `kubectl` commands
            - Delayed Pod scheduling
            - Slow controller reconciliation
            - API request timeouts
            - Frequent leader elections
            - Cluster instability
            
            ---
            
            # etcd Performance Pipeline
            
            Every request travels through multiple components.
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Leader
            
            ↓
            
            RAFT
            
            ↓
            
            WAL
            
            ↓
            
            MVCC
            
            ↓
            
            BoltDB
            
            ↓
            
            Disk
            
            ↓
            
            Response
            ```
            
            A bottleneck anywhere affects the entire pipeline.
            
            ---
            
            # Primary Performance Factors
            
            The largest performance factors are:
            
            ```text
            Storage
            
            Memory
            
            CPU
            
            Network
            
            Database Size
            
            Compaction
            
            Defragmentation
            ```
            
            Storage is usually the most critical.
            
            ---
            
            # Storage Performance
            
            etcd performs many:
            
            ```text
            Small
            
            Random
            
            Synchronous
            
            Writes
            ```
            
            Unlike large sequential workloads,
            
            etcd depends on **low latency**, not just high throughput.
            
            ---
            
            # SSD vs HDD
            
            One of the most important production decisions.
            
            ---
            
            ## HDD
            
            Hard Disk Drives use:
            
            ```text
            Mechanical
            
            Rotating Platters
            ```
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Read
            
            ↓
            
            Move Head
            
            ↓
            
            Rotate Disk
            
            ↓
            
            Read Data
            ```
            
            Every operation requires physical movement.
            
            ---
            
            # HDD Characteristics
            
            Advantages:
            
            - Large capacity
            - Lower cost
            
            Disadvantages:
            
            - High latency
            - Low random IOPS
            - Mechanical wear
            - Poor performance under RAFT workloads
            
            ---
            
            # SSD
            
            Solid State Drives use:
            
            ```text
            Flash Memory
            ```
            
            No moving parts.
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Read
            
            ↓
            
            Flash Memory
            
            ↓
            
            Return Data
            ```
            
            Nearly instantaneous access.
            
            ---
            
            # SSD Characteristics
            
            Advantages:
            
            - Very low latency
            - High random IOPS
            - Fast fsync operations
            - Excellent durability under etcd workloads
            - Lower leader commit latency
            
            Disadvantages:
            
            - Higher cost
            - Limited write endurance (typically not an issue for enterprise SSDs)
            
            ---
            
            # Performance Comparison
            
            | Storage | HDD | SSD |
            |----------|-----|-----|
            | Random Read | Slow | Fast |
            | Random Write | Very Slow | Very Fast |
            | fsync | High Latency | Low Latency |
            | WAL Performance | Poor | Excellent |
            | Production Recommendation | No | Yes |
            
            ---
            
            # Why SSDs Matter
            
            Remember RAFT.
            
            Every committed write requires:
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            Leader
            
            ↓
            
            Write WAL
            
            ↓
            
            fsync
            
            ↓
            
            Replicate
            
            ↓
            
            Commit
            ```
            
            If fsync takes:
            
            ```text
            40 ms
            ```
            
            instead of:
            
            ```text
            2 ms
            ```
            
            Every write becomes slower.
            
            ---
            
