            Many engineers assume:
            
            ```text
            More Memory
            
            ↓
            
            Faster Database
            ```
            
            Partially true.
            
            Memory helps because:
            
            - BoltDB uses memory mapping.
            - Frequently accessed pages remain cached.
            - Fewer disk reads occur.
            - Watch processing becomes more efficient.
            
            ---
            
            # Memory Architecture
            
            ```text
            RAM
            
            ↓
            
            Memory-Mapped BoltDB
            
            ↓
            
            Frequently Used Pages
            
            ↓
            
            Fast Access
            ```
            
            The operating system page cache plays a significant role.
            
            ---
            
            # Low Memory Problems
            
            Insufficient memory may lead to:
            
            ```text
            Page Faults
            
            ↓
            
            Disk Reads
            
            ↓
            
            Higher Latency
            ```
            
            Result:
            
            ```text
            Slow API Server
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Memory Example
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Database Size
            
            8 GB
            ```
            
            Available memory:
            
            ```text
            512 MB
