            # Compaction Strategy
            
            Compaction directly affects:
            
            - Database growth
            - Watch history
            - Storage usage
            - Memory consumption
            
            ---
            
            # Aggressive Compaction
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Very Short Retention
            ```
            
            Advantages:
            
            - Smaller history
            - Lower storage usage
            
            Disadvantages:
            
            - More watch restarts
            - More LIST operations
            - More API Server work
            
            ---
            
            # Relaxed Compaction
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Long Retention
            ```
            
            Advantages:
            
            - Easier watch recovery
            - Longer historical availability
            
            Disadvantages:
            
            - Larger database
            - More storage usage
            - More memory pressure
            
            ---
            
            # Production Balance
            
            A good strategy balances:
            
            ```text
            Storage
            
            ↓
            
            History
            
            ↓
            
            Recovery
            ```
            
            Neither extreme is desirable.
            
            ---
            
            # Defragmentation Schedule
            
            Remember:
            
            Compaction creates:
            
            ```text
            Free Pages
            ```
            
            Defragmentation removes them.
            
            ---
            
            # Too Frequent Defragmentation
            
            ```text
            Every Hour
            ```
            
            Problems:
            
            - Extra I/O
            - Higher CPU
            - Maintenance overhead
            - Unnecessary disruption
            
            ---
            
            # Too Rare Defragmentation
            
            ```text
            Never
            ```
            
            Problems:
            
            ```text
            Huge Database
            
            ↓
            
            Large Free Space
            
            ↓
            
            Storage Waste
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Production Strategy
            
            Typical workflow:
            
            ```text
            Monitor Fragmentation
            
            ↓
            
            Threshold Reached
            
            ↓
            
            Defragment One Member
            
            ↓
            
            Verify Health
            
            ↓
            
            Repeat
            ```
            
            Maintenance should be driven by observed fragmentation rather than arbitrary schedules.
            
