            ---
            
            # Real Production Example
            
            Suppose an e-commerce platform experiences a flash sale.
            
            Within one minute:
            
            ```text
            5,000 Pods
            
            Created
            ```
            
            The Scheduler must:
            
            - Read cached cluster state
            - Process thousands of Pods
            - Filter hundreds of Nodes
            - Score candidates
            - Bind Pods quickly
            - Keep API Server load low
            
            This is why the Scheduler relies heavily on caches, queues, watches, and plugins.
            
            ---
            
            # Production Best Practices
            
            ✔ Run multiple Scheduler replicas for high availability.
            
            ✔ Keep Scheduler close to the API Server to minimize latency.
            
            ✔ Monitor scheduling latency.
            
            ✔ Monitor queue depth.
            
            ✔ Avoid excessive custom scheduling logic.
            
            ✔ Keep Scheduler Cache synchronized through Informers.
            
            ✔ Use Scheduler Profiles instead of maintaining separate scheduler binaries when possible.
            
            ✔ Monitor failed scheduling events.
            
