            # Common Misconceptions
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 1
            
            The Scheduler starts containers.
            
            Wrong.
            
            The kubelet starts containers after the Pod is bound.
            
            ---
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 2
            
            The Scheduler talks directly to etcd.
            
            Wrong.
            
            Like other control-plane components, it communicates through the API Server.
            
            ---
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 3
            
            The Scheduler continuously polls the API Server.
            
            Wrong.
            
            It uses Informers and Watches.
            
            ---
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 4
            
            Scheduling is random.
            
            Wrong.
            
            Scheduling is a multi-stage optimization process.
            
            ---
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 5
            
            Every Pod is immediately scheduled.
            
            Wrong.
            
            Pods may wait in queues, backoff, or remain unschedulable.
            
            ---
            
            ### ❌ Misconception 6
            
            Only one scheduling algorithm exists.
            
            Wrong.
            
            Modern Kubernetes uses a plugin-based Scheduling Framework with multiple extension points.
            
