            # What is the Scheduling Cycle?
            
            One of the biggest misconceptions is:
            
            > **Scheduling means assigning a Pod to a Node.**
            
            That is only partially correct.
            
            Scheduling is actually divided into **two major phases**:
            
            ```text
            Scheduling Cycle
            
            ↓
            
            Binding Cycle
            ```
            
            The Scheduling Cycle **chooses** a Node.
            
            The Binding Cycle **commits** that decision.
            
            ---
            
            # Simple Definition
            
            The Scheduling Cycle is:
            
            > **The process of evaluating the cluster and selecting the most appropriate Node for an unscheduled Pod.**
            
            No changes are written to the API Server yet.
            
            It is only a decision-making process.
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduling vs Binding
            
            | Scheduling Cycle | Binding Cycle |
            |------------------|---------------|
            | Finds the best Node | Assigns the Pod to that Node |
            | Runs plugins | Calls the API Server |
            | Uses Scheduler Cache | Updates Pod `spec.nodeName` |
            | Makes a decision | Persists the decision |
            | No cluster modification | Cluster state changes |
            
            ---
            
            # Why Two Separate Cycles?
            
            Imagine this workflow:
            
            ```text
            Find Node
            
            ↓
            
            Write API
            
            ↓
            
            Find Node
            
            ↓
            
            Write API
            ```
            
            Every scheduling decision would wait for API operations.
            
            Instead:
            
            ```text
            Scheduling
            
            ↓
            
            Decision
            
            ↓
            
            Binding
            
            ↓
            
            API Update
            ```
            
            This separation improves:
            
            - Throughput
            - Concurrency
            - Extensibility
            - Failure recovery
            
            ---
            
            # High-Level Scheduling Cycle
            
            ```text
            Scheduling Queue
            
            ↓
            
            Get Next Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Create Snapshot
            
            ↓
            
            PreFilter
            
            ↓
            
            Filter
            
            ↓
            
            PreScore
            
            ↓
            
            Score
            
            ↓
            
            Select Best Node
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Permit
            
            ↓
            
            Trigger Binding Cycle
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Complete Scheduler Timeline
            
            ```text
            Pod Created
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            etcd
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Event
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduler Queue
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduling Cycle
            
            ↓
            
            Best Node Selected
            
            ↓
            
            Binding Cycle
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            etcd
            
            ↓
            
            kubelet
            
            ↓
            
            Running Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Step 1 — Pod Enters Scheduling Queue
            
            Suppose a user creates:
            
            ```yaml
            apiVersion: v1
            kind: Pod
            metadata:
              name: nginx
            ```
            
            API Server stores:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            ↓
            
            etcd
            ```
            
            The Scheduler receives:
            
            ```text
            Watch Event
            ```
            
            Immediately.
            
            ---
            
            # Queue Processing
            
            The Pod enters:
            
            ```text
            Active Queue
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Head
            
            ↓
            
            Pod A
            
            ↓
            
            Pod B
            
            ↓
            
            Pod C
            ```
            
            The Scheduler picks:
            
            ```text
            Pod A
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Queue → Scheduling Cycle
            
            ```text
            Scheduling Queue
            
            ↓
            
            Pop Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Start Scheduling Cycle
            ```
            
            Everything from this point happens inside one scheduling attempt.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 2 — Create Scheduler Snapshot
            
            Before evaluating Nodes,
            
            the Scheduler creates a consistent snapshot.
            
            ```text
            Scheduler Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Snapshot
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduling Plugins
            ```
            
            All plugins see the same cluster state.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Snapshot?
            
            Imagine:
            
            During scheduling,
            
            another Pod starts.
            
            Without a snapshot:
            
            ```text
            Plugin A
            
            Sees
            
            Old State
            
            Plugin B
            
            Sees
            
            New State
            ```
            
            Decision becomes inconsistent.
            
            Snapshots prevent this.
            
            ---
            
            # Snapshot Contents
            
            A Scheduler Snapshot typically contains:
            
            ```text
            Nodes
            
            Running Pods
            
            Requested Resources
            
            Allocatable Resources
            
            Images
            
            Volumes
            
            Topology Information
            ```
            
            This data remains stable during the scheduling cycle.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 3 — PreFilter Phase
            
            The first plugin stage is:
            
            ```text
            PreFilter
            ```
            
            Runs:
            
            ```text
            Once
            
            Per Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Purpose of PreFilter
            
            PreFilter performs preparation.
            
            Examples:
            
            - Calculate total CPU request
            - Calculate total memory request
            - Parse affinity rules
            - Parse topology constraints
            - Validate scheduling metadata
            
            Instead of repeating work later.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Pod requests:
            
            ```yaml
            resources:
              requests:
                cpu: 4
                memory: 8Gi
            ```
            
            PreFilter computes:
            
            ```text
            CPU Needed
            
            ↓
            
            4
            
            Memory Needed
            
            ↓
            
            8Gi
            ```
            
            Stored for later phases.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 4 — Filter Phase
            
            Now the Scheduler evaluates every candidate Node.
            
            Question:
            
            ```text
            Can
            
            This Pod
            
            Run Here?
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Filter Execution
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Cluster
            
            ↓
            
            Node1
            
            Node2
            
            Node3
            
            Node4
            ```
            
            Each Filter Plugin runs against every Node.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Node resources:
            
            ```text
            Node1
            
            2 CPU
            
            ↓
            
            Reject
            
            Node2
            
            8 CPU
            
            ↓
            
            Pass
            
            Node3
            
            4 CPU
            
            ↓
            
            Pass
            
            Node4
            
            No Disk
            
            ↓
            
            Reject
            ```
            
            Remaining:
            
            ```text
            Node2
            
            Node3
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Multiple Filter Plugins
            
            Filtering is collaborative.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            NodeResourcesFit
            
            ↓
            
            NodeAffinity
            
            ↓
            
            TaintToleration
            
            ↓
            
            VolumeBinding
            
            ↓
            
            PodTopology
            ```
            
            Every plugin must agree.
            
            One rejection removes the Node.
            
            ---
            
            # Filter Workflow
            
            ```text
            Candidate Node
            
            ↓
            
            Plugin 1
            
            ↓
            
            Plugin 2
            
            ↓
            
            Plugin 3
            
            ↓
            
            Pass?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Next Phase
            ```
            
            Otherwise:
            
            ```text
            Rejected
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Parallel Filtering
            
            Large cluster:
            
            ```text
            500 Nodes
            ```
            
            Scheduler does not evaluate them sequentially.
            
            Instead:
            
            ```text
            500 Nodes
            
            ↓
            
            Parallel Workers
            
            ↓
            
            Filter Results
            ```
            
            Massively improving throughput.
            
            ---
            
            # What if Every Node Fails?
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Node1
            
            Reject
            
            Node2
            
            Reject
            
            Node3
            
            Reject
            ```
            
            No candidates remain.
            
            Scheduler enters:
            
            ```text
            PostFilter
            ```
            
            Which may:
            
            - Trigger preemption
            - Retry later
            - Mark the Pod as unschedulable
            
            ---
            
            # Step 5 — PreScore Phase
            
            Candidate Nodes now exist.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Node2
            
            Node3
            ```
            
            Before scoring,
            
            PreScore prepares calculations.
            
            Runs:
            
            ```text
            Once
            
            Per Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why PreScore?
            
            Suppose:
            
            Topology spread requires:
            
            ```text
            Current Zone Counts
            ```
            
            Rather than calculating repeatedly,
            
            PreScore computes it once.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 6 — Score Phase
            
            Now Kubernetes answers:
            
            > **Among all valid Nodes, which one is the best?**
            
            Unlike Filter:
            
            ```text
            Pass
            
            or
            
            Fail
            ```
            
            Score produces:
            
            ```text
            Number
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Scores:
            
            ```text
            Node2
            
            88
            
            Node3
            
            94
            ```
            
            Winner:
            
            ```text
            Node3
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Multiple Score Plugins
            
            Each plugin generates its own score.
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            NodeResourcesBalancedAllocation
            
            80
            
            ImageLocality
            
            100
            
            TopologySpread
            
            70
            
            NodeAffinity
            
            90
            ```
            
            Framework combines them.
            
            ---
            
            # Score Aggregation
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```text
            Node
            
            ↓
            
            Plugin Scores
            
            ↓
            
            Weights Applied
            
            ↓
            
            Final Score
            
            ↓
            
            Winner
            ```
            
            Highest score wins.
            
            ---
            
            # Example Calculation
            
            ```text
            Node A
            
            Plugin1
            
            80
            
            Plugin2
            
            90
            
            Plugin3
            
            70
            
            ↓
            
            Final
            
            240
            ```
            
            Node B:
            
            ```text
            90
            
            95
            
            85
            
            ↓
            
            270
            ```
            
            Node B wins.
            
            (The actual framework performs normalization and weighting, but this illustrates the concept.)
            
            ---
            
            # Step 7 — Select Best Node
            
            After all scores are calculated:
            
            ```text
            Highest Score
            
            ↓
            
            Selected Node
            ```
            
            Example:
            
            ```text
            Node3
            ```
            
            Decision made.
            
            Still:
            
            ```text
            Nothing Written
            
            To API Server
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Step 8 — Reserve Phase
            
            Now the Scheduler reserves resources.
            
            Purpose:
            
            Prevent another scheduling cycle from selecting the same resources simultaneously.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Reserve?
            
            Imagine:
            
            Two Pods.
            
            One Node.
            
            Available:
            
            ```text
            4 CPU
            ```
            
            Pod A:
            
            ```text
            Needs
            
            4 CPU
            ```
            
            Pod B:
            
            ```text
            Needs
            
            4 CPU
            ```
            
            Without reservation:
            
            Both could choose:
            
            ```text
            Node1
            ```
            
            Race condition.
            
            ---
            
            # Reserve Workflow
            
            ```text
            Best Node
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Continue
            ```
            
            Reservation exists only inside the Scheduler until binding succeeds or fails.
            
            ---
            
            # Reservation Failure
            
            Suppose:
            
            Reserve Plugin fails.
            
            Scheduler performs:
            
            ```text
            Unreserve
            
            ↓
            
            Retry
            ```
            
            Cluster remains consistent.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 9 — Permit Phase
            
            Permit is optional.
            
            Purpose:
            
            Allow plugins to:
            
            ```text
            Approve
            
            Reject
            
            Wait
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Gang Scheduling.
            
            Need:
            
            ```text
            8 Pods
            
            Together
            ```
            
            Permit waits.
            
            ```text
            Pods Ready?
            
            ↓
            
            No
            
            ↓
            
            Wait
            ```
            
            Later:
            
            ```text
            Approve
            ```
            
            Scheduling continues.
            
            ---
            
            # Permit Outcomes
            
            ```text
            Approve
            
            ↓
            
            Binding
            
            Reject
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduling Failed
            
            Wait
            
            ↓
            
            Pause
            ```
            
            Only approved Pods continue.
            
            ---
            
            # Step 10 — Trigger Binding Cycle
            
            Scheduling is complete.
            
            The Scheduler now has:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Best Node
            ```
            
            Next:
            
            ```text
            Trigger
            
            Binding Cycle
            ```
            
            This hands control to the next phase.
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduling Cycle Ends Here
            
            The Scheduling Cycle finishes after:
            
            ```text
            Node Selected
            
            ↓
            
            Reserved
            
            ↓
            
            Permitted
            ```
            
            The Binding Cycle performs:
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Bind
            
            ↓
            
            Persist
            ```
            
            We'll study that in the next chapter.
            
