            # What is Binding?
            
            Binding is:
            
            > **The process of assigning a Pod to a selected Node by updating Kubernetes through the API Server.**
            
            Scheduling decides:
            
            ```text
            Which Node?
            ```
            
            Binding records:
            
            ```text
            This Pod
            
            Runs Here
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Simple Analogy
            
            Imagine booking an airline ticket.
            
            Finding a seat:
            
            ```text
            Seat 18A
            
            ↓
            
            Decision
            ```
            
            Printing the boarding pass:
            
            ```text
            Seat Reserved
            
            ↓
            
            Official
            ```
            
            Scheduling is choosing the seat.
            
            Binding is printing the boarding pass.
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduling vs Binding
            
            | Scheduling Cycle | Binding Cycle |
            |------------------|---------------|
            | Selects Node | Assigns Node |
            | Uses Scheduler Cache | Updates API Server |
            | Internal decision | Persistent cluster state |
            | No API modification | API object changes |
            | Ends with selected Node | Ends with assigned Pod |
            
            ---
            
            # High-Level Binding Flow
            
            ```text
            Scheduling Cycle
            
            ↓
            
            Best Node Selected
            
            ↓
            
            Binding Cycle
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            etcd
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Event
            
            ↓
            
            kubelet
            
            ↓
            
            Container Runtime
            
            ↓
            
            Running Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Separate Binding?
            
            Imagine Kubernetes performed:
            
            ```text
            Filter
            
            ↓
            
            API Update
            
            ↓
            
            Score
            
            ↓
            
            API Update
            ```
            
            Thousands of unnecessary writes.
            
            Instead:
            
            ```text
            Complete Scheduling
            
            ↓
            
            One API Write
            ```
            
            This reduces:
            
            - API Server load
            - etcd writes
            - Network traffic
            - Lock contention
            
            ---
            
            # Beginning of the Binding Cycle
            
            Suppose the Scheduler has selected:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            ↓
            
            frontend
            
            ↓
            
            worker-02
            ```
            
            Binding starts immediately.
            
