            # Bind Retry Logic
            
            Kubernetes does not immediately give up.
            
            Typical flow:
            
            ```text
            Binding Failed
            
            ↓
            
            Release Reservation
            
            ↓
            
            Update Scheduler State
            
            ↓
            
            Requeue Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Retry Scheduling
            ```
            
            The next scheduling attempt starts from the beginning.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Re-run Scheduling?
            
            Imagine:
            
            Node selected:
            
            ```text
            worker-5
            ```
            
            Five seconds later:
            
            ```text
            Resources Changed
            ```
            
            The previous decision may no longer be valid.
            
            Therefore Kubernetes performs:
            
            ```text
            Fresh Scheduling Cycle
            ```
            
            instead of blindly retrying the old binding.
            
