            - How Assumed Pods prevent race conditions during binding
            - The performance optimizations that allow Kubernetes to schedule Pods efficiently in large production clusters
            
            The Scheduler Cache is one of the key reasons Kubernetes can scale to thousands of Nodes while maintaining low scheduling latency. It acts as the Scheduler's "working memory," enabling rapid placement decisions based on a continuously updated view of the cluster.
            
