            # Assumed Pod
            
            One of the key concepts in the Reserve phase is the:
            
            ```text
            Assumed Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # What Is an Assumed Pod?
            
            An Assumed Pod is:
            
            > **A temporary Scheduler-side record indicating that a Pod is expected to run on a Node, even though binding has not yet completed.**
            
            ---
            
            # Why Assume?
            
            Imagine:
            
            ```text
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Binding
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Network Delay
            ```
            
            During that delay,
            
            another scheduling cycle starts.
            
            Without an assumed Pod:
            
            ```text
            Resources
            
            Appear Free
            ```
            
            Incorrect.
            
            ---
            
            # Assumed Pod Workflow
            
            ```text
            Selected Node
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Create Assumed Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Update Scheduler Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Bind
            
            ↓
            
            Binding Success
            
            ↓
            
            Assumption Confirmed
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Reservation Lifecycle
            
            Every reservation follows a lifecycle.
            
            ```text
            Node Selected
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Assumed Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Permit
            
            ↓
            
            Bind
            
            ↓
            
            API Success
            
            ↓
            
            Reservation Becomes Real
            ```
            
            If anything fails:
            
            ```text
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Rollback
            
            ↓
            
            Resources Released
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduler Cache Updates
            
            Reserve modifies:
            
            ```text
            Scheduler Cache
            ```
            
            Specifically:
            
            ```text
            NodeInfo
            
            ↓
            
            Requested Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Available Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Assumed Pods
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Before:
            
            ```text
            worker-8
            
            Requested CPU
            
            10
            ```
            
            Reserve:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            Needs
            
            2 CPU
            ```
            
            After:
            
            ```text
            worker-8
            
            Requested CPU
            
            12
            ```
            
            Again,
            
            only inside the Scheduler Cache.
            
            ---
            
            # NodeInfo Changes
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```text
            NodeInfo
            
            Before
            
            CPU Requested
            
            10
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            CPU Requested
            
            12
            ```
            
            Future scheduling cycles immediately observe:
            
            ```text
            12 CPU Requested
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Update the Cache First?
            
            Because scheduling is highly concurrent.
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            500 Pods
            
            Scheduling
            
            At Once
            ```
            
            Every scheduling cycle depends on an accurate view of resource availability.
            
            The Scheduler Cache provides that view.
            
            ---
            
            # Reservation Failure
            
            Not every reservation succeeds.
            
            Possible reasons include:
            
            - Plugin failure
            - Internal Scheduler error
            - Invalid reservation
            - External reservation failure
            - Custom plugin rejection
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Custom GPU plugin:
            
            ```text
            GPU License
            
            Unavailable
            ```
            
            Reserve Plugin returns:
            
            ```text
            Failure
            ```
            
            Scheduling stops.
            
            ---
            
            # Another Example
            
            External hardware allocator:
            
            ```text
            Reserve FPGA
            
            ↓
            
            Allocation Failed
            ```
            
            Reservation cannot continue.
            
            ---
            
            # Reservation Failure Flow
            
            ```text
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Failure
            
            ↓
            
            Rollback
            
            ↓
            
            Pod Requeued
            ```
            
            The Pod is **not** bound.
            
            ---
            
            # Rollback
            
            If Reserve fails,
            
            the Scheduler must undo every temporary change.
            
            This is called:
            
            ```text
            Rollback
            ```
            
            In the Scheduling Framework,
            
            this is performed through:
            
            ```text
            Unreserve
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Unreserve Plugin
            
            The framework provides:
            
            ```text
            Unreserve()
            ```
            
            Purpose:
            
            ```text
            Undo Reservation
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Rollback Workflow
            
            ```text
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Update Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Failure
            
            ↓
            
            Unreserve
            
            ↓
            
            Restore Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Retry Scheduling
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Before Reserve:
            
            ```text
            CPU Free
            
            8
            ```
            
            Reserve:
            
            ```text
            CPU Free
            
            4
            ```
            
            Failure occurs.
            
            Rollback:
            
            ```text
            CPU Free
            
            8
            ```
            
            Cluster state returns to normal.
            
            ---
            
            # Reservation Lifecycle Diagram
            
            ```text
            Scheduling Finished
            
            ↓
            
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Assumed Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduler Cache Updated
            
            ↓
            
            Permit
            
            ↓
            
            Bind
            
            ↓
            
            Success
            
            ↓
            
            Reservation Confirmed
            ```
            
            Failure path:
            
            ```text
            Reserve
            
            ↓
            
            Failure
            
            ↓
            
            Unreserve
            
            ↓
            
            Remove Assumed Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Restore Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Requeue Pod
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Reserve vs Bind
            
            | Reserve | Bind |
            |----------|------|
            | Internal Scheduler operation | API Server operation |
            | Updates Scheduler Cache | Updates Pod object |
            | Temporary | Persistent |
            | Prevents race conditions | Commits scheduling decision |
            | Reversible | Cluster state changes |
            
