            # Scheduler Startup
            
            When a Custom Scheduler starts,
            
            it typically performs:
            
            ```text
            Connect API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Start Informers
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Pods
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Nodes
            
            ↓
            
            Watch PersistentVolumes
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Other Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Begin Scheduling Loop
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduler API
            
            The Scheduler does not communicate directly with Nodes.
            
            Instead,
            
            everything happens through:
            
            ```text
            Kubernetes API Server
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduler API Responsibilities
            
            The Scheduler reads:
            
            - Pods
            - Nodes
            - PersistentVolumes
            - PersistentVolumeClaims
            - PriorityClasses
            - CSINodes
            - RuntimeClasses
            - StorageClasses
            
            The Scheduler writes:
            
            - Pod Binding
            - Events
            - Leader Election information (if enabled)
            
            ---
            
            # API Interaction
            
            ```text
            Custom Scheduler
            
                    │
            
                    ▼
            
            API Server
            
                    │
            
             ┌──────┼──────────┐
            
             ▼      ▼          ▼
            
            Pods   Nodes    Storage
            ```
            
            The API Server is the single source of truth.
            
            ---
            
            # Watching Pods
            
            Scheduling begins by watching for:
            
            ```text
            Pending Pods
            ```
            
            The Scheduler continuously observes:
            
            ```text
            Pod Added
            
            ↓
            
            Pending
            
            ↓
            
            schedulerName Matches?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Schedule
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Watch-Based Architecture
            
            Instead of polling:
            
            ```text
            Every 5 Seconds
            
            ↓
            
            Check Pods
            ```
            
            Kubernetes uses:
            
            ```text
            Watch
            
            ↓
            
            Instant Notification
            ```
            
            This provides low scheduling latency.
            
            ---
            
            # Pod Watch Workflow
            
            ```text
            User Creates Pod
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Watch Event
            
            ↓
            
            Custom Scheduler
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduling Starts
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Watching Nodes
            
            The Scheduler also watches:
            
            ```text
            Node Added
            
            Node Updated
            
            Node Deleted
            ```
            
            Why?
            
            Because scheduling decisions depend on:
            
            - Available CPU
            - Available Memory
            - Labels
            - Taints
            - Conditions
            - Capacity
            - Allocatable Resources
            
            ---
            
            # Scheduler Cache
            
            Like the default Scheduler,
            
            a custom Scheduler typically maintains an internal cache.
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Informers
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduler Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Scheduling Decisions
            ```
            
            This avoids querying the API Server for every Pod.
            
            ---
            
            # Selecting Nodes
            
            Once a Pending Pod is received,
            
            the Scheduler performs:
            
            ```text
            Candidate Discovery
            
            ↓
            
            Filtering
            
            ↓
            
            Scoring
            
            ↓
            
            Best Node
            ```
            
            This logic is entirely customizable.
            
            ---
            
            # Example
            
            Cluster:
            
            ```text
            Node A
            
            GPU
            
            Node B
            
            CPU
            
            Node C
            
            GPU
            ```
            
            Incoming Pod:
            
            ```text
            Requires GPU
            ```
            
            Scheduler:
            
            ```text
            Filter
            
            ↓
            
            Node A
            
            Node C
            
            ↓
            
            Score
            
            ↓
            
            Choose Node A
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Selection Workflow
            
            ```text
            Pending Pod
            
            ↓
            
            List Nodes
            
            ↓
            
            Apply Scheduling Rules
            
            ↓
            
            Rank Nodes
            
            ↓
            
            Best Node
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Binding Pods
            
            After selecting a Node,
            
            the Scheduler commits the decision.
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Selected Node
            
            ↓
            
            Binding Request
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Pod Updated
            
            ↓
            
            kubelet Watch
            
            ↓
            
            Container Starts
            ```
            
            This is the same Binding process used by the default Scheduler.
            
