            The Reconciliation Loop is the engine that makes Kubernetes self-healing and declarative. Every built-in Controller—from Deployments and ReplicaSets to Jobs and StatefulSets—uses this same pattern to continuously drive the cluster toward the user's desired state, ensuring that the actual system converges on the intended configuration despite failures, updates, and ongoing change.
            
