            Database
            
            Cache
            
            Certificate
            
            AIModel
            
            KafkaCluster
            ```
            
            Who will manage these resources?
            
            Kubernetes itself does not know how.
            
            We need to build our own controller.
            
            The standard framework for this is:
            
            ```text
            controller-runtime
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why controller-runtime Exists
            
            Originally,
            
            developers built controllers directly using:
            
            ```text
            client-go
            ```
            
            This required manually implementing:
            
            - Informers
            - Shared caches
            - WorkQueues
            - Event handlers
            - Leader election
            - Watches
            - Reconciliation loop
            - Error handling
            - Metrics
            - Health checks
            
            Building everything from scratch became repetitive.
            
            ---
            
            # Kubernetes Solution
            
            The Kubernetes ecosystem introduced:
            
            ```text
            controller-runtime
            ```
            
            It provides reusable controller infrastructure.
            
            Instead of writing:
            
            ```text
            5000+
            
            Lines
            
            Of Boilerplate
            ```
            
            developers primarily implement:
            
            ```text
            Reconcile()
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # High-Level Architecture
            
            ```text
                             Manager
            
                                │
            
                 ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
            
                 ▼              ▼              ▼
            
              Cache         Client        Controller
            
                                                  │
            
                                           Reconciler
            
                                                  │
            
                                           Kubernetes API
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # What is controller-runtime?
            
            controller-runtime is:
            
            > **A high-level Go framework built on top of client-go that simplifies building Kubernetes Controllers and Operators.**
            
            It is **not** part of the Kubernetes API Server.
            
            It is a Go library used by controller applications.
            
            ---
            
            # Major Components
            
            ```text
            Manager
            
            Cache
            
            Client
            
            Reconciler
            
            Builder
            
            Watches
            
            Predicates
            
            Controller
            ```
            
            These components work together to implement reconciliation.
            
            ---
            
            # Overall Architecture
            
            ```text
                         Manager
            
                    ┌──────┼──────┐
            
                    ▼      ▼      ▼
            
                 Cache   Client  Controller
            
                                    │
            
                                Builder
            
                                    │
            
                                Watches
            
                                    │
            
                               Predicates
            
                                    │
            
                              WorkQueue
            
                                    │
            
                              Reconciler
            
                                    │
            
                                 API Server
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Manager
            
            The Manager is the heart of controller-runtime.
            
            Everything starts here.
            
            ---
            
            # Responsibilities
            
            The Manager is responsible for:
            
            - Starting Controllers
            - Starting Shared Caches
            - Creating Clients
            - Leader Election
            - Metrics Server
            - Health Endpoints
            - Webhooks (if configured)
            - Lifecycle management
            
            ---
            
            # Conceptually
            
            ```text
            Manager
            
            ↓
            
            Starts
            
            Everything
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Manager Architecture
            
            ```text
                         Manager
            
                            │
            
                ┌───────────┼────────────┐
            
                ▼           ▼            ▼
            
             Cache      Controller    Webhooks
            
                            │
            
                      Reconciler
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why One Manager?
            
            Suppose we have:
            
            ```text
            Database Controller
            
            Certificate Controller
            
            Kafka Controller
            
            Backup Controller
            ```
            
            Instead of:
            
            ```text
            4
            
            Independent Processes
            ```
            
            One Manager can host multiple Controllers within the same process.
            
            ---
            
            # Manager Startup
            
            ```text
            Create Manager
            
            ↓
            
            Start Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Wait Cache Sync
            
            ↓
            
            Leader Election
            
            ↓
            
            Start Controllers
            
            ↓
            
            Start Workers
            ```
            
            Controllers begin reconciliation only after caches are synchronized.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache
            
            controller-runtime heavily relies on:
            
            ```text
            Shared Cache
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Cache?
            
            Imagine:
            
            ```text
            100 Controllers
            
            ↓
            
            Every Controller
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            ```
            
            The API Server would become overloaded.
            
            ---
            
            # Instead
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Shared Informers
            
            ↓
            
            Local Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Controllers Read Cache
            ```
            
            Most reads are served from memory.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Architecture
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Informer
            
            ↓
            
            Local Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Reconciler
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Synchronization
            
            At startup:
            
            ```text
            List
            
            ↓
            
            Populate Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Watch
            
            ↓
            
            Incremental Updates
            ```
            
            This matches the Shared Informer pattern discussed earlier.
            
            ---
            
            # Benefits
            
            - Reduced API traffic
            - Faster reads
            - Shared memory
            - Better scalability
            - Lower etcd load
            
            ---
            
            # Client
            
            The Client is the interface used by Reconcilers.
            
            Example operations:
            
            ```text
            Get
            
            List
            
            Create
            
            Update
            
            Patch
            
            Delete
            
            Status Update
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Split Client
            
            The default controller-runtime Client is often called a **split client**.
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```text
            Reads
            
            ↓
            
            Cache
            
            Writes
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            ```
            
            This provides efficient reads while ensuring writes go directly to the authoritative API.
            
            ---
            
            # Client Architecture
            
            ```text
            Reconciler
            
            ↓
            
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            Read?
            
            ↓
            
            Cache
            
            ----------------
            
            Write?
            
            ↓
            
            API Server
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Reads Use Cache
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            1000 Reconciliations
            
            Per Second
            ```
            
            Reading directly from the API Server every time would create unnecessary load.
            
            Cached reads are much more efficient.
            
            ---
            
            # Reconciler
            
            The Reconciler contains:
            
            ```text
            Business Logic
            ```
            
            Everything else exists primarily to support this function.
            
            ---
            
            # The Reconcile Function
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```go
            Reconcile(Request)
            
            ↓
            
            Observe
            
            ↓
            
            Compare
            
            ↓
            
            Act
            ```
            
            This follows the Kubernetes reconciliation pattern.
            
            ---
            
            # Reconcile Architecture
            
            ```text
            WorkQueue
            
            ↓
            
            Worker
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile()
            
            ↓
            
            Read Objects
            
            ↓
            
            Compare Desired
            
            ↓
            
            Apply Changes
            
            ↓
            
            Return Result
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Inputs
            
            Reconcile receives:
            
            ```text
            Namespaced Name
            ```
            
            Not the entire object.
            
            The Reconciler retrieves the latest object using the Client.
            
            ---
            
            # Typical Workflow
            
            ```text
            Receive Request
            
            ↓
            
            Read Resource
            
            ↓
            
            Resource Exists?
            
            ↓
            
            Yes
            
            ↓
            
            Compare State
            
            ↓
            
            Need Change?
            
            ↓
            
            Apply Changes
            
            ↓
            
            Done
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Idempotency
            
            The Reconcile function should be:
            
            ```text
            Idempotent
            ```
            
            Meaning:
            
            Running it:
            
            ```text
            1 Time
            
            or
            
            100 Times
            ```
            
            Produces the same desired state.
            
            ---
            
            # Builder
            
            Creating Controllers manually is verbose.
            
            Instead,
            
            controller-runtime provides:
            
            ```text
            Builder Pattern
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Builder Responsibilities
            
            Builder configures:
            
            - Primary resource
            - Secondary resources
            - Watches
            - Predicates
            - Event handlers
            
            before creating the Controller.
            
            ---
            
            # Builder Workflow
            
            ```text
            Builder
            
            ↓
            
            Configure Watches
            
            ↓
            
            Configure Predicates
            
            ↓
            
            Create Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Register Manager
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Example Concept
            
            ```text
            Controller
            
            Watches
            
            Database
            
            ↓
            
            Owns
            
            Pods
            
            ↓
            
            Owns
            
            Services
            ```
            
            Builder expresses these relationships declaratively.
            
            ---
            
            # Watches
            
            Controllers react to:
            
            ```text
            Events
            ```
            
            Examples:
            
            ```text
            Create
            
            Update
            
            Delete
            
            Generic
            ```
            
            These are called:
            
            ```text
            Watches
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Watch Architecture
            
            ```text
            API Server
            
            ↓
            
            Informer
            
            ↓
            
            Event
            
            ↓
            
            Watch
            
            ↓
            
            WorkQueue
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Watches?
            
            Without Watches:
            
            ```text
            Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Poll
            
            ↓
            
            Every Second
            ```
            
            Very inefficient.
            
            Instead:
            
            ```text
            Event Driven
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Primary Watch
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Database CR
            ```
            
            Changes.
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Database Updated
            
            ↓
            
            Event
            
            ↓
            
            Queue
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Secondary Watch
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            Deleted
            ```
            
            The controller may need to reconcile:
            
            ```text
            Database
            ```
            
            Secondary Watches map child object events back to the owning resource.
            
            ---
            
            # Predicates
            
            Not every event requires reconciliation.
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Status Updated
            ```
            
            Should reconciliation occur?
            
            Maybe not.
            
            Predicates filter events.
            
            ---
            
            # Predicate Architecture
            
            ```text
            Watch Event
            
            ↓
            
            Predicate
            
            ↓
            
            Accept?
            
             │
            
             ├── Yes
            
             │
            
             ▼
            
            Queue
            
             │
            
             └── No
            
                  │
            
                  ▼
            
            Ignore
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Why Predicates?
            
            Without Predicates:
            
            ```text
            Every Event
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile
            ```
            
            Potentially thousands of unnecessary reconciliations.
            
            ---
            
            # Common Predicate Examples
            
            Only reconcile when:
            
            - Spec changes
            - Labels change
            - Generation changes
            
            Ignore:
            
            - Status-only updates
            - Metadata updates that are irrelevant
            
            Filtering improves performance.
            
            ---
            
            # Event Flow
            
            ```text
            Object Updated
            
            ↓
            
            Watch
            
            ↓
            
            Predicate
            
            ↓
            
            WorkQueue
            
            ↓
            
            Worker
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile()
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Custom Controllers
            
            The real purpose of controller-runtime is enabling:
            
            ```text
            Custom Controllers
