            # Image Registry
            
            Images are stored in registries.
            
            Examples:
            
            ```text
            Docker Hub
            
            GHCR
            
            Quay
            
            Harbor
            
            Amazon ECR
            
            Google Artifact Registry
            
            Azure Container Registry
            ```
            
            The runtime communicates directly with the registry.
            
            ---
            
            # Registry Architecture
            
            ```text
            Container Runtime
            
            ↓
            
            Registry API
            
            ↓
            
            Manifest
            
            ↓
            
            Layer Download
            
            ↓
            
            Local Cache
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Manifest Download
            
            The runtime first downloads:
            
            ```text
            Manifest
            ```
            
            The manifest contains:
            
            - Layer digests
            - Image configuration
            - Architecture
            - Platform
            
            Only after reading the manifest does the runtime know which layers to fetch.
            
            ---
            
            # Layer Download
            
            Each layer is downloaded independently.
            
            ```text
            Layer 1
            
            ↓
            
            Layer 2
            
            ↓
            
            Layer 3
            
            ↓
            
            Layer 4
            ```
            
            Previously downloaded layers are reused.
            
            ---
            
            # Image Verification
            
            Before storing an image,
            
            containerd verifies:
            
            ```text
            SHA256 Digest
            
            ↓
            
            Integrity Check
            ```
            
            Corrupted downloads are rejected.
            
            ---
            
            # Image Cache
            
            Downloaded images remain on the Node.
            
            ```text
            Registry
            
            ↓
            
            Download
            
            ↓
            
            Local Cache
            
            ↓
            
            Future Pods
            
            ↓
            
            Reuse
            ```
            
            This dramatically reduces startup time.
            
            ---
            
            # Cache Example
            
            First Pod:
            
            ```text
            Image Missing
            
            ↓
            
            Download
            
            ↓
            
            45 Seconds
            ```
            
            Second Pod:
            
            ```text
            Image Cached
            
            ↓
            
            2 Seconds
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Local Storage
            
            containerd stores:
            
            ```text
            Image Layers
            
            ↓
            
            Content Store
            
            ↓
            
            Snapshots
            
            ↓
            
            Metadata
            ```
            
            Images persist until removed.
            
            ---
            
            # Image Pull Policy
            
            Image Pull Policy controls when Kubernetes requests an image pull.
            
            Three values exist:
            
            ```text
            Always
            
            IfNotPresent
            
            Never
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # IfNotPresent
            
            Default for most tagged images.
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Image Cached?
            
            │
            
            ├── Yes
            
            │
            
            ▼
            
            Use Cache
            
            │
            
            └── No
            
                 │
            
                 ▼
            
            Pull Image
            ```
            
            Most production workloads use this behavior.
            
            ---
            
            # Always
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Pod Starts
            
            ↓
            
            Check Registry
            
            ↓
            
            Pull If Needed
            
            ↓
            
            Run Container
            ```
            
            The runtime still avoids downloading unchanged layers because it compares image digests.
            
            ---
            
            # Never
            
            Workflow:
            
            ```text
            Image Cached?
            
            │
            
            ├── Yes
            
            │
            
            ▼
            
            Run
            
            │
            
            └── No
            
                 │
            
                 ▼
            
            Fail
            ```
            
            Useful for air-gapped environments or preloaded images.
            
            ---
            
            # Pull Policy Comparison
            
            | Policy | Behavior |
            |----------|----------|
            | Always | Always checks the registry before starting the container |
            | IfNotPresent | Uses cached image if available |
            | Never | Never contacts a registry |
            
            ---
            
            # Default Behavior
            
            Important interview question.
            
            ```text
            Image
            
            nginx:latest
            
            ↓
            
            Default
            
            Always
            ```
            
            ```text
            Image
            
            nginx:1.27
            
            ↓
            
            Default
            
            IfNotPresent
            ```
            
            The special `:latest` tag defaults to `Always`; other tagged images default to `IfNotPresent` if no pull policy is specified.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Avoid :latest?
            
            Production deployments should avoid:
            
            ```text
            latest
            ```
            
            Because:
            
            ```text
            Today
            
            ↓
            
            Version A
            
            ────────────
            
            Tomorrow
            
            ↓
            
            Version B
            ```
            
            Deployments become non-reproducible.
            
            Prefer immutable version tags or image digests.
            
