            ---
            
            # Why Multiple Runtimes?
            
            Different applications require different trade-offs.
            
            Some require:
            
            ```text
            Maximum Performance
            ```
            
            Others require:
            
            ```text
            Maximum Isolation
            ```
            
            RuntimeClass enables this flexibility.
            
            ---
            
            # Runtime Comparison
            
            Conceptually:
            
            ```text
            Performance
            
            runc
            
            >
            
            gVisor
            
            >
            
            Kata (varies by workload)
            
            ────────────
            
            Isolation
            
            Kata
            
            >
            
            gVisor
            
            >
            
            runc
            ```
            
            No runtime is universally best.
            
            ---
            
            # runc
            
            runc is the default OCI runtime used by most Kubernetes clusters.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Container
            
            ↓
            
            Linux Namespaces
            
            ↓
            
            Linux Kernel
            ```
            
            Advantages:
            
            - Fast startup
            - High performance
            - Mature ecosystem
            
            Limitations:
            
            - Shares the host kernel with containers
            
            ---
            
            # Kata Containers
            
            Kata Containers provide stronger isolation.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            ↓
            
            Kata Runtime
            
            ↓
            
            Lightweight VM
            
            ↓
            
            Guest Kernel
            
            ↓
            
            Application
            ```
            
            Each Pod runs inside its own lightweight virtual machine.
            
            ---
            
            # Why Kata?
            
            Traditional containers share:
            
            ```text
            Host Kernel
            ```
            
            Kata introduces:
            
            ```text
            Dedicated Guest Kernel
            ```
            
            This significantly improves isolation.
            
            ---
            
            # Kata Workflow
            
            ```text
            Pod
            
            ↓
            
            containerd
            
            ↓
            
            Kata Runtime
            
            ↓
            
            Create VM
            
            ↓
            
            Boot Guest Kernel
            
            ↓
            
            Start Container
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Kata Advantages
            
            - Strong isolation
            - Hardware virtualization
            - Better multi-tenant security
            - Reduced kernel attack surface
            
            Trade-offs:
            
            - Higher memory usage
            - Slower startup than runc
            - Additional virtualization overhead
            
            ---
            
            # gVisor
            
            gVisor takes a different approach.
            
            Instead of using a VM,
            
            it introduces a userspace kernel.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Application
            
            ↓
            
            gVisor
            
            ↓
            
            Host Kernel
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # gVisor Workflow
            
            ```text
            Application
            
            ↓
            
            System Call
            
            ↓
            
            gVisor
            
            ↓
            
            Host Kernel
            ```
            
            Many system calls are intercepted by gVisor before reaching the host kernel.
            
            ---
            
            # Why gVisor?
            
            Goal:
            
            ```text
            Reduce
            
            Kernel Attack Surface
            ```
            
            Applications have less direct interaction with the host kernel.
            
            ---
            
            # gVisor Advantages
            
            - Stronger isolation than runc
            - Lower overhead than full virtualization
            - Good balance between security and performance
            
            Trade-offs:
            
            - Some workloads experience performance overhead
            - Not every Linux feature is supported
            
            ---
            
            # Runtime Comparison Table
            
            | Runtime | Isolation | Performance | Startup Time | Typical Use Case |
            |----------|-----------|-------------|--------------|------------------|
            | runc | Standard container isolation | Highest | Fastest | General workloads |
            | gVisor | Stronger userspace isolation | Medium | Moderate | Untrusted applications |
            | Kata Containers | Hardware-assisted isolation | Lower than runc for many workloads | Slowest | Multi-tenant and highly sensitive workloads |
            
