            # Where This Chapter Fits
            
            In previous chapters we learned:
            
            ```text
            Client
            
            ↓
            
            ClusterIP
            
            ↓
            
            iptables/IPVS
            
            ↓
            
            Backend Pod
            ```
            
            But one important question remains:
            
            > **How does Kubernetes ensure that every packet of the same TCP connection reaches the same Pod?**
            
            Suppose:
            
            ```text
            Packet 1
            
            ↓
            
            Pod A
            
            ────────────
            
            Packet 2
            
            ↓
            
            Pod B
            ```
            
            Would the TCP connection work?
            
            No.
            
            TCP requires every packet in a connection to reach the same endpoint.
            
            Linux solves this problem using:
            
            ```text
            conntrack
