            # What is Operator SDK?
            
            Operator SDK is an open-source framework for building, testing, packaging, and distributing Kubernetes Operators.
            
            It extends the Operator development workflow by providing:
            
            - Project scaffolding
            - Testing
            - Packaging
            - Bundle generation
            - OLM integration
            - Operator distribution
            
            Unlike Kubebuilder,
            
            Operator SDK focuses not only on development but also on the **Operator lifecycle**.
            
            ---
            
            # Operator SDK Architecture
            
            ```text
                           Operator SDK CLI
            
                                  │
            
                                  ▼
            
                      Generates Project Structure
            
                                  │
            
                                  ▼
            
                        controller-runtime
            
                                  │
            
                                  ▼
            
                          Kubernetes Operator
            
                                  │
            
                                  ▼
            
                      OLM / Kubernetes Cluster
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Operator SDK vs Kubebuilder
            
            This is one of the most common interview questions.
            
            | Kubebuilder | Operator SDK |
            |-------------|--------------|
            | Official Kubernetes scaffolding framework | Framework built on top of Kubebuilder and controller-runtime |
            | Focuses on API and Controller generation | Focuses on Operator development and lifecycle |
            | Generates project boilerplate | Adds packaging, bundles, OLM support, testing |
            | Primarily developer-focused | Developer + Operations focused |
            
            Today,
            
            Go-based Operators created using Operator SDK typically rely on the same `controller-runtime` library used by Kubebuilder.
            
            ---
            
            # High-Level Architecture
            
            ```text
            Developer
            
            ↓
            
            Operator SDK
            
            ↓
            
            Project
            
            ↓
            
            Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Manager
            
            ↓
            
            controller-runtime
            
            ↓
            
            Kubernetes
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Types of Operators
            
            Operator SDK supports multiple Operator styles.
            
            ```text
            Operator SDK
            
            ├──────── Go Operator
            
            ├──────── Helm Operator
            
            └──────── Ansible Operator
            ```
            
            Each style serves different use cases.
            
            ---
            
            # Go Operators
            
            The most powerful Operator type.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            CRD
            
            ↓
            
            Go Controller
            
            ↓
            
            Reconcile()
            
            ↓
            
            Kubernetes API
            ```
            
            Features:
            
            - Full programming flexibility
            - Custom reconciliation logic
            - External API integration
            - Advanced workflows
            - Maximum performance
            
            Suitable for:
            
            - Database Operators
            - Cloud Infrastructure Operators
            - Networking Operators
            - Storage Operators
            
            ---
            
            # Helm Operators
            
            Instead of writing Go code,
            
            the Operator manages Helm charts.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Custom Resource
            
            ↓
            
            Helm Chart
            
            ↓
            
            Rendered Templates
            
            ↓
            
            Kubernetes Resources
            ```
            
            The reconciliation process applies Helm releases based on the Custom Resource.
            
            ---
            
            # Helm Operator Workflow
            
            ```text
            User Creates CR
            
            ↓
            
            Operator
            
            ↓
            
            Render Helm Chart
            
            ↓
            
            Install Resources
            
            ↓
            
            Monitor Changes
            
            ↓
            
            Upgrade Release
            ```
            
            Ideal when applications already have mature Helm charts.
            
            ---
            
            # Advantages of Helm Operators
            
            - Minimal Go programming
            - Reuse existing Helm charts
            - Faster Operator development
            - Easier application packaging
            
            Limitations:
            
            - Less flexible than Go Operators
            - Complex business logic is harder to implement
            
            ---
            
            # Ansible Operators
            
            Instead of Go,
            
            business logic is implemented using Ansible.
            
            Architecture:
            
            ```text
            Custom Resource
            
            ↓
            
            Ansible Playbooks
            
            ↓
            
            Kubernetes Resources
            ```
            
            Best suited for infrastructure automation teams already using Ansible.
            
            ---
            
            # Ansible Operator Workflow
            
            ```text
            Custom Resource
            
            ↓
            
            Operator
            
            ↓
            
            Execute Playbook
            
            ↓
            
            Configure Infrastructure
            
            ↓
            
            Update Status
            ```
            
            ---
            
            # Comparing Operator Types
            
            | Feature | Go | Helm | Ansible |
            |---------|----|-------|----------|
            | Programming Language | Go | Helm Templates | Ansible |
            | Flexibility | High | Medium | Medium |
            | Performance | High | High | Lower for complex automation |
            | External API Integration | Excellent | Limited | Good |
            | Learning Curve | Higher | Lower | Lower (for Ansible users) |
            
